  "world": {
   "notes": "This save is set in the world of Breaking Bad, before Gus Fring's death: Los Pollos Hermanos is a chain of fourteen fried-chicken restaurants across the Southwest, founded by Gus and Max Arciniega and now a subsidiary of the German conglomerate Madrigal Electromotive, which holds a stake. It is also the front for the biggest methamphetamine distribution network in the region: product from a superlab under an industrial laundry travels in the chain's refrigerated trucks inside fry-batter buckets. The restaurants themselves are kept spotless and legitimate. The DEA is circling, and the Juárez cartel wants the business back. The slogan is \"where something delicious is always cooking\". The menu reflects what the show's menu boards carry (fried chicken, burritos, enchiladas, tacos, fry bread, green chile stew, curly fries, churros, apple bites, shakes), but the prices are set for 2009 and are not from the show. Keep the tone of the show: controlled, quiet, and very dangerous. Never describe how drugs are made; the back room is business, people and consequences.",
